#%PAM-1.0
# Tilo's one sign-in service (docs/security/sign-in.md §5.2). The greeter
# (greetd), the lock screen (tilo-unlock), polkit (polkit-1, which run0 and
# pkexec authenticate through) and sudo take their auth, account and password
# phases from here and keep only their own session phase, so every surface
# accepts the same factors.
#
# 1. The boot sign-in: in the greeter's service only, whoever opened the
#    system volume at boot starts their session without typing again, once.
# 2. A fingerprint, only while tilo-authd holds the person's key for a session
#    of theirs running now (the lock screen, polkit and sudo inside it, the
#    greeter when switching back to them). After boot, or once their sessions
#    have ended, a fingerprint is not offered: a match unwraps nothing, so it
#    may only confirm someone whose key is already in memory (§4.3). The
#    pam_tilo step decides; when it cannot, the fingerprint step is skipped.
# 3. The secret: password-auth, where pam_tilo asks tilo-authd before the old
#    password check (os/scripts/authselect-tilo.py).
-auth      sufficient                  pam_tilo.so boot_sign_in=greetd
auth       [success=ignore default=1]  pam_tilo.so fingerprint
-auth      sufficient                  pam_fprintd.so
auth       substack                    password-auth

account    include                     password-auth

password   substack                    password-auth
